{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/535203-2nd-ed-game-play-question","id":535203,"title":"2nd ed game play question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-31T21:48:00-07:00","id":535203,"title":"2nd ed game play question","content":"Last week I set aside money and, with great excitement, made the jump to 2 ed. I have been getting ready to play in my first WtF game in nearly ten years. I have run many games, but no one else ever wanted to tackle being the GM in my group till now. I can't explain how excited I am to play a character I have had in my head for over five years.<br /> <br /> Looking at 2nd edition I really liked the changes, until I got to the gifts and facets. Don't get me wrong, I like the idea and many of them are great, but it looks like Irraka and Rahu have a <i>huge </i>leg up compared to everyone else. It appears that the Cunning and Purity facets are among the best for almost every list as I was looking. I understand that these two Auspices are the most battle centered but it is a little discouraging if you want to play something else. Almost every facet I was looking at tied to Wisdom matched a one or two dot gift in the original book.<br /> <br /> Most noticeably it appears that the shaman type of play that was available to Ithaeur has been eliminated completely. The Elemental and Weather gifts just do not have the same power that they previously had and now with the new limitation on the facets what you do have is based on what Renown you are working with, and again, Wisdom seems to get little help in combat situations.<br /> <br /> I know that the game is not all combat, but if you are playing a tabletop game then you know that even combat light sessions are going to have a focus on the fights, that is one of the reasons we play after all. My question for those who have been playing, how balanced does it come out when all is said and done? <br /> <br /> I have wanted to play a shaman caster Ithaeur for years but after looking at what this book has to offer I just don't see that it can be done anymore. I am also concerned after looking at Killer Instinct and the rest of the Full Moon's Gift set that if the Rahu in the party decides to do something, no one can stop her. Yeah, Rahu are suppose to be battle focused but that one dot just seems crazy. <br /> <br /> I am feeling really discouraged and was hoping some of you could give me insights on how the game play has been going in 2nd edition. <br /> <br /> \u200bThanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T23:01:39-07:00","id":535264,"title":"","content":"If you're looking to play a blaster mage Werewolf I think the book may disappoint you. I don't think that's a major part of the idea of what a werewolf can do in this game. If you do want to play a kind of Ithaeur Shaman, however, you will probably have to rely on the Tribal Affinities. Personally, I think the Insight and Knowledge Gifts are exceptionally useful. The Nature gifts are really cool for a Protector of the Wilds sort of Shaman. I'm not sure if Beast Ride works on human beings, though I don't think it specifically says no, and that would be a pretty cool effect.<br /> <br /> If you go Iron Master, the Technology gifts make for a cool Technomancer type character (and the Shaping gifts, especially Unmake, don't hurt).<br /> <br /> The Death Gift of course is fantastic across the board if you're going for that kind of character. Sort of a traditional Witch Doctor type Shaman. Very thematic. Absorbing damage from packmates. Getting answers from corpses. Ability to see into twilight and damage the undead. I think the Purity facet is the only one in that Gift that isn't exceptional.<br /> <br /> And I'm very surprised to hear you say that the Weather gifts aren't as strong. I would beg to differ. The 1E Weather gifts were useless until the 4th and 5th dots, and in my opinion the Elemental gift is really strong once you get around 4 and 5 renown, especially if you are creative enough. As strong as anything from 1E. You really do become a blaster mage at that point.<br /> <br /> Your argument about the Rahu is correct in some ways. No one is supposed to stop a Rahu physically except another Rahu. And maybe an Irraka who plays his cards right. But those are their roles. The Rahu is going to outshine his packmates when it comes down to hitting things hardest, but that's his area. Everyone has their area. Your Ithaeur is still a werewolf and the pack is working together, not competing against each other. And there are so many ways for the Ithaeur to shine. The Iron Master Ithaeur in my group already Unmade a sports car as our prey was escaping in it, dismantling it completely. Used Iron Slave to send a truck barreling through the police station to break our Irraka out of jail, and used a rite to erase all video evidence of a giant Uratha vs. Azlu brawl that happened (partially) in a Bank parking lot. If that isn't cool, I don't know what is.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that Purity is the Rahu's auspice renown, but it's not his alone. If you think the Purity renown is strongest, your Ithaeur, as a Shaman, will probably have more than a couple dots of renown there anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 06-01-2015, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T23:17:32-07:00","id":535278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/535203-2nd-ed-game-play-question?p=535264#post535264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Purity facet is the only one in that Gift that isn't exceptional.</div> </div> </div> </div>For contrast, I note that Bone Gnaw replicates the effect of the Stillness Oracle that a Sin-Eater character of mine tended to use as an interrogation tool.<br /> <br /> Somebody thinks a secret is important enough to keep from you? Make it known that killing them lets you get that info <i>more easily</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T02:59:36-07:00","id":535403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Face_Plont</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/535203-2nd-ed-game-play-question#post535203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am feeling really discouraged and was hoping some of you could give me insights on how the game play has been going in 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> \u200bThanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's ok, do you think you could expand on what you mean by 'the shaman type of play' and 'a shaman caster Ithaeur'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T03:10:11-07:00","id":535404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Face_Plont</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/535203-2nd-ed-game-play-question#post535203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Elemental and Weather gifts just do not have the same power that they previously had <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure with Catastrophe, Heart of Water and about 3 dots of wisdom you could cause a tsunami. <br /> <br /> Or with Flesh of Earth, flip a city over like a pancake. <br /> <br /> And with the purity one, how about just setting fire to everything? Mass create. Everything is on fire. <br /> <br /> Breath of air. Hello tornado. <br /> <br /> And as for weather, are you kidding me? That lot can shut someone down completely at high enough levels, and as long as you have Hunt Under Iron Skies you're totally unaffected. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Face_Plont</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/535203-2nd-ed-game-play-question#post535203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wisdom seems to get little help in combat situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, aside from the aforementioned waterbending, (seriously, get in a lake and just drown everyone) Wisdom gifts let you figure out where your prey is headed so you can intercept them, warg into animals like, say, a rhino, turn the support beams of a building to putty, stealth at full speed and take much less damage from falling (potentially up to the point where they will walk away from any fall ever), chew through a brick wall, and telepathically communicate with your pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T09:46:06-07:00","id":535684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/535203-2nd-ed-game-play-question?p=535264#post535264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I'm very surprised to hear you say that the Weather gifts aren't as strong. I would beg to differ. The 1E Weather gifts were useless until the 4th and 5th dots, and in my opinion the Elemental gift is really strong once you get around 4 and 5 renown, especially if you are creative enough. As strong as anything from 1E. You really do become a blaster mage at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot to mention that we play with the errata version of the gifts, which makes them more worth it.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I guess I wasn't very specific enough on some of the details for my character. I wanted to play a Stormlord more blaster type, but now I am really going to need to tweak what I go with. Thinking of scratching that character completely.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I got to the gifts section last weekend while I was reading between panels at a Comicon. I went back last night and was scanning them and decided I must be missing something, which is why I asked for some opinions here. As always, this forum is fantastic and I appreciate everyone's responses. My character wont be throwing fireballs and calling lightning like I always wanted, but it looks like he will be able to do some other things fun.<br /> <br /> My last question has more to do with the Rahu. Again, I didn't make myself very clear in that I feel that the way packs usually choose their Alpha as the strongest that they have a huge leg up. Since my character has changed and I wont be that Stormlord anymore I suppose it doesn't matter, I just fear that if the Rahu is interested in being the leader, it would be really hard to beat him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T09:50:35-07:00","id":535688,"title":"","content":"In general, the ideas that 1) the pack needs an Alpha and 2) it has to be the strongest aren't necessarily true. The pack will usually pick their own alpha based on &quot;popular vote&quot;, or just shift the alpha around as necessary. Heck, maybe there won't even be an alpha and nobody leads the pack except when there's a hunt on (and then it'd be whoever called the hunt).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T10:00:35-07:00","id":535691,"title":"","content":"I think it's neat how different people see different renown as 'the best,' and how they rate the power of assorted gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Elemental and Weather gifts just do not have the same power that they previously had and now with the new limitation on the facets what you do have is based on what Renown you are working with </div> </div> </div>First edition had more limitations, as you couldn't have a Gift worth more dots than your highest primary Renown. So you couldn't get those 4 and 5 dot gifts until you had your 4 and 5 dots in a primary Renown.<br /> <br /> The Elemental Gifts are pretty much the same as they were, except as I pointed out, easier to get and with Catastrophe. The mechanics for the first edition gifts were really ambiguous, as it suggested you could use any element in any gifts spot, but it didn't offer a good example for what, for instance, the fire element version of 'Invoke the Wind's Wrath' was. Now they offer a straight Influence, allowing you to do your basic damage if you want, as well as many utilitarian usages. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts\">We've had at least one thread exploring the things one can do with the elemental gifts.</a><br /> <br /> As for the Weather Gifts, you're right in that they aren't exactly, 'Hit a target and do extra damage,' they do carry the potential to essentially create natural disasters, and while I hate this term, it's great for debuffs. Hunt of Fire and Ice, the Wisdom facet, can just destroy people outside, and you can ensure people can't find a way inside with the Cunning facet. Repeated use of Heavens Unleashed can have very serious results. For these you can just look at actual natural disasters and see what happens, right now there's massive flooding in Texas and a tremendous heat wave in India.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wanted to play a Stormlord more blaster type, but now I am really going to need to tweak what I go with. </div> </div> </div>Or you can just go Elemental. Until 4 dots in Renown you need a source for fire, like a lighter, which you can turn into a blast of dragon's breath. But at 4 and 5 you can breathe fire yourself. From there you could just get a fetish like the Storm Coil to give you Influence of electricity in the same way you have it over fire.<br /> <br /> With the fourth Crescent Gift, as well, you can just take a spirit's influences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I didn't make myself very clear in that I feel that the way packs usually choose their Alpha as the strongest that they have a huge leg up. </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily how they choose their alpha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T10:02:28-07:00","id":535693,"title":"","content":"The idea of packs having alphas at all is a 1e convention. Not to say a pack *cant* have an alpha in 2e, but it's literally never mentioned in the book, so it would be the choice of the individual pack, not something that is traditionally part of every pack's structure. Even if your ST wants to make that kind of pack model a default part of his setting, it makes just as much sense for the most spirtually enlightened member to lead as it does for the strongest to lead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T10:07:14-07:00","id":535697,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are quite capable of comprehending that the best at hitting people is not always the best at deciding who to hit. I could easily see a tough bruiser who knows he's not a paragon in the brains department deferring to the less direct smart guy for tactical advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T10:14:12-07:00","id":535700,"title":"","content":"Thing worth pointing out from last year's Gifts thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117729#post117729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second is a more general note for the thread - I got rid of what we termed 'Killing You Gifts'. Things like Thunderbolt and Killing Frost - powers that involve the werewolf pointing and throwing magic at a target to kill them, mage-style - are generally gone. Instead, the new Facets that focus on making the werewolf better at killing make them superior at doing so up close and personal, with claws and teeth and weapons. A werewolf doesn't call lightning down to strike you with a Facet; a Facet gives a werewolf the ability to tear through steel like it was butter, or to hack you apart like a joint of meat with each strike crippling you in a horrific new fashion.<br /> <br /> I have, however, kept Facets with effects under what we classify as the old 'Killing Your City Gifts' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T10:25:06-07:00","id":535709,"title":"","content":"I guess Charlaquin really hit by stating that Alphas are not mentioned in 2E. To be fair, none of the many games I have run had an Alpha who was technically the physically strongest, I was just thinking about pecking order as I was reading all of these gifts. My whole mindset seems to still be in the old version where a lot of emphasis was put on the pecking order.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T12:47:01-07:00","id":535829,"title":"","content":"Yeah, pecking order is about as important to werewolves as it is to humans. Which is to say, it can be very important, especially in tight knit social groups, but it is not all-consuming. A Pack is very much like a gang. There is probably some form of social hierarchy, and it may or may not be enforced by strength and dominance. But at the end of the day, werewolves have the minds of humans, and their social structures are therefore as varied and nuanced as human social structures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T16:03:32-07:00","id":536035,"title":"","content":"I still worry about that one dot Full Moon gift that gives 8 again for one essence. That just seems absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T16:44:25-07:00","id":536145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Face_Plont</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/535203-2nd-ed-game-play-question?p=536035#post536035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still worry about that one dot Full Moon gift that gives 8 again for one essence. That just seems absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, while 8-again may look sexy, mathematically it's actually less beneficial than you might think. Second, compare it to the other 1 dot Moon Gift Facets, though.<br /> <br /> Crescent Moon gives you + Wisdom on Empathy rolls against spirits for a scene and reveals a spirit's Ban or Bane for 1 Essence (both on an exceptional success). That gives you a tremendous amount of leverage against the spirit for social maneuvering, <i>and</i> a huge advantage in combat against it. Plus you can spend additional Essence to learn the Bans and Banes of any spirit that may be present in the scene. Note that this is the kind of information you would normally have to go on entire quests to learn.<br /> <br /> Gibbous Moon gives your whole pack +1 damage to all Brawl and Weaponry attacks for several turns for 1 Essence. Depending on the size of the pack, that will most likely add up to more total damage than the Rahu's 8-again will add.<br /> <br /> Half-Moon gives you flawless lie detection for a full scene for 1 Essence.<br /> <br /> New Moon gives you the Rote quality on a sneak attack for 1 Essence. Unlike 8-again, Rote quality is amazing, borderline broken in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T16:54:56-07:00","id":536157,"title":"","content":"I will yield to your understanding on this Charlaquin. I just have several bad experiences with players in the past who were one shooting things when given exploding 8+. I know that the math shouldn't be too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:10:17-07:00","id":536238,"title":"","content":"Oh, one shotting of things will definitely happen against lesser opponents. That's the new baseline for Werewolves; humans, animals, low-rank Spirits, they're all speed bumps at most. But against other werewolves, high-rank spirits, powerful ridden, and he hosts, you're going to <i>need</i> all that extra damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T04:57:20-07:00","id":536807,"title":"","content":"Regarding eight again, what it's useful for is guys with a decent pool to begin with. More successes on average will mean more chance for the eight again to hit in. The Rahu in the pack should be able to scary things in combat, it's their job.<br /> <br /> I found embracing the high power level and moving the average challenge's goalpost made for more epic play. Besides, if a player's put a load of dots into combat, they're entitled to use it.<br /> <br /> Players can be awesome, eight again helps the awesome become.... More awesome, okay I've run out of words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:07:43-07:00","id":565872,"title":"","content":"First I wanted to say thanks again to this awesome community. I have my Ithaeur and am completely sold on 2E because you guys gave me such wonderful ideas.<br /> <br /> I have a new problem, well it isn't me this time but another player. He wants to make a silent killer Irraka, shouldn't be hard right? I keep telling him to go with Blood Talons but he is obsessing over the purity gifts and insists that they are the only way to be strong. Of course that means he has to go Hunters but then he doesn't have access to strength and rage gifts. He is currently trying to convince the GM just to let him use the gifts from 1E. Honestly, he is being a pain in the ass and I have already told him once that if he wants to make a Rahu just to make a Rahu.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions? I am again assuming that everyone here has more experience so what would you tell this player? He's not usually this much of a pain in the ass, I think if I just nudge him a bit in the right direction he will be happier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:21:31-07:00","id":565884,"title":"","content":"Why do you keep telling him to go Blood Talon? Don't get me wrong, an Irraka Blood Talon could be awesome, but let him make his character the way he wants. Why does he feel Purity Facets are the only way to be strong? There are lots of great Facets for every Renown; particularly if he wants to make a silent killer type, most of the best Facets for stealth-focused characters are associated with Cunning, in my opinion. And if he does want to go with a heavy focus on Purity, why would he need to play a Hunter in Darkness? I mean, Irraka Hunter in Darkness can make an extremely potent stealth killer, and it's my favorite combination. But any character can gain Purity Renown, so if that's his only reason for going Hunter in Darkness, it seems like an odd choice to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:40:42-07:00","id":565888,"title":"","content":"Alright, so, I glazed over the issue. He wanted to go Blood Talon. We are making starting characters and he is obsessing over the Purity facets because he sees them as the only way to &quot;do more damage.&quot; He is only focusing on abilities he think will do damage. We are fresh characters, our GM said we get some xp and one more rank in a renown of our choice. He tried to make his character an Irraka Blood Talon with two dots in Purity and one in his two primary renown. He also only choose purity facets as his starting gifts. He got frustrated when I called him out and has dragged his feet fixing it since. <br /> <br /> I will try to get him to look at the Hunters. He is just obsessing over damage and I want him to expand his views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T18:09:27-07:00","id":565909,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you are having fun with your character. I honestly think this system is really amazing at empowering each auspice.<br /> <br /> Honestly, all you need to be a silent killer Irraka is the first moon gift and a half decent dice pool. Rote action will do most that work for you. Get the Stealth gift Cunning facet for the rote actions on stealth and no one will ever see you you coming. Add maybe the Fading merit for some additional stealth and you're in business. As far as tribe, it really doesn't matter. The irraka gift lists give you everything you need (Feet of Mist and Slip Away for making a clean get away, for example). The tribe might add to the approach.<br /> <br /> For example, the Iron Masters give access to the Technology gift facet for shutting down lights (that one <i>is</i> Purity, I think) gift which is useful for bewildering prey and making damn sure that no one sees what happened and who did it. As well as the knowledge gift for making sure you're killing the right guy (Know thy prey). The Hunters give access to a bunch of nature gifts which help if you're playing in a more rural setting, Nowhere to Hide, a merit that makes it so that no one can ever really escape a Hunter who is tracking them, and the Warding gifts - All Doors Unlocked is great for breaking and entering, or trapping your prey and keeping them right where you want them.<br /> <br /> As far as the Blood Talons, they might give you a bit more damage, and that's all well and good if that's what he wants. A Blood Talon Irraka is a consummate badass, but I think you already have the damage. If you're rolling 6-8 dice with a weapon modifier of any kind and rote action, you're going to kill most things on the first strike. Maybe you'll need a second strike to put the poor creature out of its misery before you disappear back into the shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 06-23-2015, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T20:02:11-07:00","id":565984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Face_Plont</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/535203-2nd-ed-game-play-question?p=565888#post565888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so, I glazed over the issue. He wanted to go Blood Talon. We are making starting characters and he is obsessing over the Purity facets because he sees them as the only way to &quot;do more damage.&quot; He is only focusing on abilities he think will do damage. We are fresh characters, our GM said we get some xp and one more rank in a renown of our choice. He tried to make his character an Irraka Blood Talon with two dots in Purity and one in his two primary renown. He also only choose purity facets as his starting gifts. He got frustrated when I called him out and has dragged his feet fixing it since.<br /> <br /> I will try to get him to look at the Hunters. He is just obsessing over damage and I want him to expand his views.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I just don't see what the problem is. What did you call him out on? Seems like he's making perfectly legitimate character choices to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T20:46:38-07:00","id":566015,"title":"","content":"That's a good point. If he's just creating the kind of character he wants, there shouldn't be any problem with that. If you're worry about power gaming, I think you probably shouldn't be. NWoD, even Werewolf, is a storytelling game first and foremost, and being able to kill things faster than everyone else isn't going to ruin the fun for anyone else.<br /> <br /> Sounds like you're very concerned about 'power level' in general, and there's no reason to be. If the storyteller has no problem with it in his game, don't see why you should either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T04:47:25-07:00","id":566244,"title":"","content":"Only issue I see is that the character in question can't have two dots in purity at character creation. His two primary renown would be cunning and glory, at best he could have one dot in purity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T06:41:20-07:00","id":566302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> our GM said we get some xp and one more rank in a renown of our choice </div> </div> </div>So apparently the GM is giving them extra XP and an Additional Dot of Renown. So, obviously not quite a starting character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T07:28:10-07:00","id":566339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/535203-2nd-ed-game-play-question?p=566302#post566302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So apparently the GM is giving them extra XP and an Additional Dot of Renown. So, obviously not quite a starting character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Missed that bit, but yeah no issues if he wants to make a one trick pony. Gonna have a bad time outside of combat though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:41:44-07:00","id":567028,"title":"","content":"Indeed... it is often hard to tell people that when they are unwilling to listen, or do not care about the out-of-combat scenes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T16:57:22-07:00","id":568509,"title":"","content":"I sat him down and reviewed some of the things you all suggested with him. This isn't his first time playing WoD and I ran him in a 1E WtF game but he just got really hung up on combat when making his character for some reason. He has changed his character around a bit, still heavily focused on combat but now that he gets the changes and what he can do he is pleased with his character. Thanks again everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}